# Build output
node_modules/
web/node_modules
web/dist
/target
**/*.rs.bk

# Local config — .env.example is committed, .env is not
.env

# Scratch
prototype/demo-page.html

# Lockfiles are deliberately NOT ignored. This is an application, not a library: the exact
# dependency versions are part of what makes a build reproducible, and `npm ci` refuses to
# run without one. `package-lock.json` was ignored here from before there was any code,
# which broke CI's dependency cache and would have broken `npm ci` one step later.
#   Cargo.lock             committed
#   web/package-lock.json  committed

# Python bytecode. `build-code-tour.py` imports `build.py` for the pacing constants,
# which makes CPython write one of these next to it.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The mutation harness leaves one of these beside a file while it is running. It is a
# scratch copy of your own source and must never be committed - see docs/mutations/README.md.
*.mutate-backup
